# Own-wording spells of Dark Matter (2014 rules), part B.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Eye of Anubis": ["60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 Necrotic, and the target cannot Disengage. A second beam at level 5.",
 "60 ft. A beam of dark moonlight streaks from your left eye at a creature in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 Necrotic damage and cannot take the Disengage action until the end of your next turn.\nAt level 5 you fire a second beam from your right eye. The first beam's damage becomes 2d8 at level 11, and the second beam's becomes 2d8 at level 17."],
"Eye of Ra": ["60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 Radiant, and the target cannot Hide. A second beam at level 5.",
 "60 ft. A beam of furious radiance erupts from your right eye at a creature you see in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 Radiant damage and cannot take the Hide action until the end of your next turn.\nAt level 5 you fire a second beam from your left eye. The first beam's damage becomes 2d8 at level 11, and the second beam's becomes 2d8 at level 17."],
"Finger Guns": ["Self, bonus action. Your action then makes a spell attack at 60 ft for 1d8 Force.",
 "Self, bonus action. You extend finger and thumb in a gun gesture. For the duration you can use your action to make a spell attack against a creature you see within 60 ft, dealing 1d8 Force damage on a hit. The finger gun counts as a blaster, but not as magical technology, for spells and effects that affect blasters.\nThe damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at level 11 and 4d8 at level 17."],
"Flawed Reconstruction": ["Touch. A willing creature regains 4d6 hit points, but its maximum drops by the same amount until a Long Rest.",
 "Touch. You stitch the wounds of a willing creature you touch. It regains 4d6 hit points, but the mending is imperfect: its hit point maximum drops by the same amount until it finishes a Long Rest. A creature healed by this spell is left with permanent scars." + HL + "The healing and the maximum reduction both rise by 1d6 for each slot level above 1st."],
"Geodesic Shield": ["Touch, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. A 15 ft dome with clean air blocks ranged attacks and spells. AC 10, 20 HP.",
 "Touch, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Translucent triangular plates of force form a spherical dome with a 15-ft radius, centered on a point you touch. The dome holds clean, breathable air. Poison gas, smoke and fog cannot enter, and it insulates against extreme temperatures. Creatures can walk freely in and out, but the dome blocks ranged attacks, spells and other effects. It has AC 10 and 20 HP. The spell ends when it drops to 0." + HL + "With a slot of 3rd level or higher, the dome's AC rises by 1 and its HP by 10 for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Greater Mending": ["120 ft. Repair an object up to 10 ft across, including magic items and constructs.",
 "120 ft. This spell repairs breaks, tears and other damage in an object you see in range, such as a smashed control panel, ripped radiation plating, a corrupted keycard or a jammed turbine. If the object is no larger than 10 ft in any dimension, you mend it fully with no trace of damage. It cannot restore lost hit points to a damaged ship. It can repair a magic item or construct if the object's magic was present when it broke. It does not restore lost charges."],
"Hack System": ["10,000 ft, Concentration. Two systems on a ship are disabled if its engineer fails a Wisdom save.",
 "10,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Choose a spaceship you see in range. Its engineer makes a Wisdom save, and the save automatically fails if no one holds the role. On a failure, choose two of the ship's systems. They are disabled for the duration. An engineer who is not incapacitated can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success." + HL + "With a slot of 4th level or higher, you affect one more system for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Halo of Flame": ["Self (10 ft ring). Dexterity save or 4d6 Fire damage to creatures you choose.",
 "Self (10-ft-radius ring). A ring of flame ignites above your head and springs outward into a burning circle: a line of flame 5 ft wide curving into a 10-ft-radius ring around you. Each creature you choose in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 4d6 Fire damage on a failure, or half on a success." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Hardlight Blaster": ["10 ft. A hardlight weapon fires once for 3d6 Force from its own position, then dissipates.",
 "10 ft. You wave your hand and conjure a weapon of compressed light that hovers in an unoccupied space within 10 ft. It fires a beam at a target you choose within 60 ft of it, as a ranged spell attack using your spell attack bonus. The weapon is the origin of the attack, so it can target a creature outside your line of sight if the weapon can see it. On a hit the target takes 3d6 Force damage. After the attack the weapon dissipates." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 1st."],
"Hardlight Construction": ["30 ft, 10 minutes. Build a solid hardlight object up to a 15 ft cube, AC 10, HP 30 + your spellcasting modifier.",
 "30 ft, 10 minutes. You compress light into a solid structure within range. It can be a Huge or smaller object, in a 15-ft cube or 27 connected 5-ft cubes, such as a bridge over a chasm, a lookout tower or a starship hull patch. It has no moving parts and cannot directly harm anyone. It has AC 10 and HP equal to 30 + your spellcasting modifier. It collapses and the spell ends if it drops to 0 HP." + HL + "With a slot of 4th level or higher, its HP rises by 10 per slot level above 3rd. With a slot of 6th level or higher, you can use your action to change it into any other object that fits the limits. This does not restore its HP."],
"Hardlight Frame": ["Self, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Power armor: AC 16, 40 temporary HP, Large, 2d12 Force battlefists, two attacks.",
 "Self, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Plates of compressed light swarm your body into a suit of power armor. For the duration: your AC is 16 if it was lower. You gain 40 temporary hit points. If they drop to 0 the spell ends, and any left over when it ends are lost. Your size is Large if it was smaller. You have Advantage on Strength checks and saves. The armor works as a life suit. It has two integrated battlefists you are proficient with, used as melee spell attacks against a target within 10 ft, dealing 2d12 + your spellcasting ability modifier Force damage. You attack twice with the Attack action, unless you already have Extra Attack or a similar feature." + HL + "The temporary hit points rise by 10 for each slot level above 5th."],
"Hardlight Gauntlet": ["Touch. Three melee spell attacks on one target for 1d12, 2d12 and 3d12 Force.",
 "Touch. You conjure a gauntlet of compressed energy and unleash a barrage. Make three melee spell attacks against one target. The first hit deals 1d12 Force damage, the second 2d12 and the third 3d12." + HL + "With a slot of 5th level or higher you make 1 more attack, and the fourth hit deals 4d12. With a slot of 7th level or higher you make 2 more attacks, and the fifth hit deals 5d12."],
"Hardlight Nails": ["60 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. A 10 ft square of hardlight spikes: difficult terrain, 2d6 Force per 5 ft moved, and a 4d6 line burst.",
 "60 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Thousands of tiny spikes of light form in a 10-ft square on a surface you choose in range. The area is difficult terrain. A creature moving in it takes 2d6 Force damage for every 5 ft it travels.\nAs a reaction when a creature moves directly in front of the spikes, out to 30 ft, you can make them explode outward and end the spell. Each creature in a line 30 ft long and 10 ft wide from the spikes makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d6 Force damage on a failure, or half on a success."],
"Hardlight Needle": ["60 ft. A target takes 3 Piercing damage.",
 "60 ft. You condense light into a razor-sharp point you guide with ease. A target you see in range takes 3 Piercing damage.\nThe damage becomes 6 at level 5, 9 at level 11 and 12 at level 17."],
"Hold Ship": ["5,000 ft, Concentration. A ship's speed and maneuverability drop to 0 and its weapons cannot fire.",
 "5,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Choose a spaceship you see in range. Its engineer makes a Wisdom save, and the save automatically fails if no one holds the role. On a failure the ship's speed and maneuverability are 0 for the duration and its mounted weapons cannot fire. An engineer at their station who is not incapacitated can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success."],
"Intensify Gravity": ["100 ft, Concentration. A 50 ft radius, 100 ft high cylinder where movement costs double and ranged attacks have Disadvantage.",
 "100 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Gravity grows in a cylinder 50 ft in radius and 100 ft high, centered on a point in range. Each creature in it spends 2 ft of movement per foot moved, including flying, jumping and climbing. With difficult terrain this slows movement to a quarter. A prone creature must succeed on a Strength check against your spell save DC to stand, and on a failure cannot move that turn.\nObjects there, worn or carried, weigh double, which can encumber creatures or break load-bearing spells like levitate. Ranged weapon attacks into, out of or through the area have Disadvantage, and falling damage in the area is doubled."],
"Logic Bomb": ["30 ft, Concentration. Disable magical technology, and stop constructs that fail a Wisdom save.",
 "30 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Circuits of arcane energy reach from your fingertips into nearby technology and spread a magical virus. Unattended magical technology you choose in range is disabled for the duration. Each creature you choose that wears or carries magical technology, or has embedded technology, must succeed on an Intelligence (Technology) check against your spell save DC at the start of each of its turns or be unable to use it. On a success the spell ends for that target.\nEach construct you choose in range makes a Wisdom save, with Advantage if it is a living construct such as a vect. On a failure it cannot move and is Incapacitated, even if normally immune, for the duration. At the start of each of its turns it can repeat the save, ending the effect on a success."],
"Magic Mic": ["Self. A spectral microphone amplifies and distorts your voice, reaches 10 miles by radio, and shouts for 1d4 Thunder.",
 "Self, bonus action. You conjure a spectral microphone that hovers before you or is held in one hand. Speaking through it makes your voice boom and lets you distort it: change its pitch, add an echo, make it metallic, add static or any simple audio effect. It cannot fully copy another person's voice. You can change the volume and distortion on your turn with no action. Your voice also carries over radio waves, heard on comm sets and communication systems within 10 miles.\nYou can use your action to shout into the mic. Each creature you choose within 10 ft makes a Constitution save or takes 1d4 Thunder damage.\nThe damage becomes 2d4 at level 5, 3d4 at level 11 and 4d4 at level 17."],
}
